From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shiny <owner@shinychang.net>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:36:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: build in Talk to Shy, a side panel for chatting with an
 agent

- A component extension with a fixed id opens in the side panel from its
  toolbar button or the palette command "Talk to Shy: Show or Hide Panel".
- It keeps a WebSocket open to a relay: agents reach it over MCP to list
  tabs, read pages and run WebMCP tools, and chat goes to an OpenAB agent.
- Any site can be used by default. A WebMCP tool that changes the page
  asks first, and "Always allow here" remembers the answer.
- The toolbar button is pinned once, so unpinning it sticks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYkQJUafT3hpFT1kBmDgzX
